# 🔹 Concept: Insert at End
When we insert a new node at the end:
1. Create a new node.  
2. If the list is empty → that new node **becomes the head**.  
3. Otherwise, traverse until the last node (`next == NULL`).  
4. Make the last node’s `next` point to the new node.  

Think of it as **adding someone to the end of the line**.  

---

# 🔹 Code: Insert at End

```c
// Insert a new node at the end
void insertAtEnd(struct Node** head, int value) {
    struct Node* newNode = createNode(value);

    if (*head == NULL) {
        // If list is empty, new node becomes head
        *head = newNode;
        return;
    }

    struct Node* temp = *head;
    while (temp->next != NULL) {  // Traverse until last node
        temp = temp->next;
    }

    temp->next = newNode;  // Link last node to new node
}
```

